      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Figure 2: Overview of the SWE-Debate framework showing three interconnected stages: (1) Fault Propagation Traces Proposal, which extracts initial entities from the issue description (e.g., get_foo_bar_display, FooBar, get_FIELD_display) and traverses the static dependency graph along Contain, Inherit, Import, and Invoke edges to generate localization chains 1..N; (2) Multi-Agent Debate, consisting of Round 1 Localization Chain Selection via competitive ranking/voting to choose the Best Chain, Round 2 Modification Plan Proposal & Competitive Refinement where N=5 agents debate alternative strategies, and Round 3 Synthesizing a concrete <plan> via a discriminator; and (3) Patch Generation via Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS), where Search, Plan, and Edit actions navigate repository states to produce the final patch.",
          "state": "draft",
